      "last_updated": "2026-08-14",
      "body": "What AI can you actually use here, today? This guide collects the AI services available to University of Idaho researchers, staff, and students — and how to get access to each one.\n\n## Campus-hosted language models\n\nMindRouter is the front door: sign in with university credentials, generate a key, and use campus GPUs from a browser chat or any standard client.\n\n{{kb: rcds-mindrouter}}\n\n{{kb: rcds-guide-mindrouter}}\n\n## Getting more out of the models\n\n{{kb: general-prompt-engineering}}\n\n## AI for research administration\n\n{{kb: iids-vandalizer-overview}}\n\n{{kb: iids-vandalizer-access}}\n\n{{kb: iids-guide-vandalizer}}\n\n## Run your own models\n\nFor model training and custom GPU workloads, the cluster is the path.\n\n{{kb: rcds-guide-gpu-computing}}\n\n## Beyond campus\n\n{{kb: rcds-external-computing-resources}}"
