      "body": "Every policy that touches IIDS work, in one list: the units' operating terms already in force, and the institute's own drafts. Entries marked Draft are under review and not yet adopted — do not cite them as institute policy yet.\n\n## In force — unit operating terms\n\n{{kb: rcds-storage-acceptable-use}}\n\n{{kb: gbrc-data-policy}}\n\n## Affiliation and access\n\n{{kb: iids-policy-affiliation-requirement}}\n\n{{kb: iids-policy-subsidized-services}}\n\n{{kb: iids-policy-code-of-conduct}}\n\n## Money\n\n{{kb: iids-policy-fa-split}}\n\n## Proposals\n\n{{kb: iids-proposal-submission-criteria}}\n\n## On their way\n\nTwo more sets of operating terms are headed into the knowledge base: the **RCDS Terms of Service** — the authoritative acceptable-use terms for the computing environment, which the Code of Conduct and eligibility drafts both point to — and the institute's **Proposal Submission Policy**, today a PDF. Until they land here, the source pages remain authoritative."
