      "visibility": "public",
      "created_date": "2026-07-17",
      "last_updated": "2026-08-10",
      "body": "Bring IIDS in early. The office prepares your proposal and routes it to the Office of Sponsored Programs (OSP) on your behalf.\n\n## Who to contact\n- **IIDS Program Manager: Mollyann Jones** — mollyannj@uidaho.edu\n- All financial and grant questions start with the Program Manager.\n\n## When to reach out\n- **At least 3 weeks** before the submission deadline.\n- **At least 4 weeks** if the proposal includes subawards or contracts.\n\n## What your email must contain\nFive things. The last two are what the request is judged on, so do not rush them.\n\n- The **RFA** — a PDF or a link.\n- The **submission deadline**.\n- A list of **PIs and Co-PIs**, including external collaborators.\n- A **brief summary** of the project, 2 to 5 sentences.\n- A **brief justification**, 2 to 5 sentences, explaining why submission through IIDS is appropriate.\n\n## It is a request, not a form\nThe IIDS Director and relevant staff evaluate every request against intellectual alignment, reliance on IIDS infrastructure and personnel, and current staff capacity. See [How IIDS evaluates a submission request](kb_entry.html?id=iids-proposal-submission-criteria).\n\n## What IIDS handles for you\n- Prepares and submits the proposal; acts as your liaison with OSP.\n- Grant reporting, grant projections, and spending plans.\n- Sponsor prior-approval requests.\n- Subaward processing.\n\nThe full pre-award and post-award list — including budget preparation, paid external pre-review, teaching release, and design support — is in [What IIDS does for a proposal](kb_entry.html?id=iids-proposal-support-services).\n\n## Where to go next\n- Who does what on your grant → you direct the research, your home department runs hiring and personnel paperwork, and the IIDS Office administers the award.\n- Who to email for what → the IIDS Program Manager, for submission, deadlines, and anything financial.\n- Spending your award → [IIDS spending rules](kb_entry.html?id=iids-spending-rules)"
