      "last_updated": "2026-08-13",
      "body": "The University of Idaho instance runs at [vandalizer.uidaho.edu](https://vandalizer.uidaho.edu/).\n\n## Try it\n\nVisit [vandalizer.uidaho.edu](https://vandalizer.uidaho.edu/) to start a self-serve **two-week trial**, and reach out through the [AI4RA contact page](https://ai4ra.uidaho.edu/contact/) to renew trial access. Research administrators at U of I and Southern Utah University are the platform's first production users, and the AI4RA team is expanding access in stages — if the trial doesn't fit your situation, the contact page is the route to a conversation.\n\n## For your institution\n\nThe Vandalizer Community Edition is open source and self-hosted: a single 16 GB server is enough, setup is a one-command interactive installer, and fully air-gapped installs (local models, local document OCR) are supported. The AI4RA team hosts **technical office hours every second Tuesday** for the IT and data staff deploying it — setup, configuration, security, and real-world infrastructure questions.\n\n## Where questions go\n\n- Access and program questions: the [AI4RA contact page](https://ai4ra.uidaho.edu/contact/)\n- Deployment help: the office hours above, and the [deployment guide](https://github.com/ui-insight/vandalizer)"
