      "id": "rcds-busco",
      "group": "RCDS",
      "title": "BUSCO",
      "gist": "Assess genome, transcriptome, or protein-set completeness by checking for expected single-copy orthologous genes using BUSCO.",
      "source": "https://hpc.uidaho.edu/compute/Applications/BUSCO.html",
      "source_url": "https://hpc.uidaho.edu/compute/Applications/BUSCO.html",
      "tags": [
        "track:applications",
        "topic:genome-assessment",
        "topic:phylogenomics"
      ],
      "entry_type": "procedural",
      "keywords": [
        "busco",
        "genome-completeness",
        "augustus",
        "orthologs",
        "gene-prediction"
      ],
      "related": [
        "rcds-augustus",
        "rcds-blast"
      ],
      "visibility": "public",
      "created_date": "2026-07-18",
      "last_updated": "2026-07-18",
      "body": "![](https://busco.ezlab.org/home/busco.png)\n\n\n\"from QC to gene prediction and phylogenomics\"\n\n[User Guide](https://busco.ezlab.org/busco_userguide.html)\n\nBUSCO is a python application, and is installed with the python/3.8.11 module. You should also load Augustus.\n\n```\nmodule load python/3.8.11 augustus\n```\n\nBusco requires a config file, here is an example for the Rocky 8 systems:\n\n```\n#\n# This is the BUSCOv4 default configuration file.\n# Rename it as config.ini and edit the path and command values to match your own environnment.\n# You can use the script busco_configurator.py to do it for you\n# Many of the options in the busco_run section can alternatively be set using command line arguments. See the help prompt (busco -h) for details.\n# WARNING: passing a parameter through the command line overrides the value specified in this file.\n#\n# You need to set the path to this file in the environment variable BUSCO_CONFIG_FILE\n# as follows:\n# export BUSCO_CONFIG_FILE=\"/path/to/myconfig.ini\"\n#\n# Enable a parameter by removing \";\"\n#\n[busco_run]\n# Input file\n;in = /path/to/input_file.fna\n# Run name, used in output files and folder\n;out = BUSCO_run\n# Where to store the output directory\n;out_path = /path/to/output_folder\n# Path to the BUSCO dataset\n;lineage_dataset = bacteria\n# Which mode to run (genome / proteins / transcriptome)\n;mode = genome\n# Run lineage auto selector\n;auto-lineage = True\n# Run auto selector only for non-eukaryote datasets\n;auto-lineage-prok = True\n# Run auto selector only for eukaryote datasets\n;auto-lineage-euk = True\n# How many threads to use for multithreaded steps\n;cpu = 16\n# Force rewrite if files already exist (True/False)\n;force = False\n# Restart a previous BUSCO run (True/False)\n;restart = False\n# Blast e-value\n;evalue = 1e-3\n# How many candidate regions (contigs, scaffolds) to consider for each BUSCO\n;limit = 3\n# Augustus long mode for retraining (True/False)\n;long = False\n# Augustus species\n;augustus_species = human\n# Augustus parameters\n;augustus_parameters='--genemodel=intronless,--singlestrand=false'\n# Quiet mode (True/False)\n;quiet = False\n# Local destination path for downloaded lineage datasets\n;download_path = ./busco_downloads/\n# Run offline\n;offline=True\n# Ortho DB Datasets version\n;datasets_version = odb10\n# URL to BUSCO datasets\n;download_base_url = https://busco-data.ezlab.org/v4/data/\n# Download most recent BUSCO data and files\n;update-data = True\n\n[tblastn]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/ncbi-blast/2.11.0/bin/\ncommand = tblastn\n\n[makeblastdb]\npath =/opt/modules/biology/ncbi-blast/2.11.0/bin/\ncommand = makeblastdb\n\n[augustus]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/augustus/3.5.3/bin/\ncommand = augustus\n\n[etraining]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/augustus/3.5.3/bin/\ncommand = etraining\n\n[gff2gbSmallDNA.pl]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/augustus/3.5.3/scripts/\ncommand = gff2gbSmallDNA.pl\n\n[new_species.pl]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/augustus/3.5.3/scripts/\ncommand = new_species.pl\n\n[optimize_augustus.pl]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/augustus/3.5.3/scripts/\ncommand = optimize_augustus.pl\n\n[hmmsearch]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/hmmer/3.2.1/bin\ncommand = hmmsearch\n\n[sepp]\npath = /home/biodocker/sepp/\ncommand = run_sepp.py\n\n[prodigal]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/prodigal/2.6.3/bin/\ncommand = prodigal\n```\n\nHere is an example for the older EL7 systems (for posterity):\n\n```\n#\n# This is the BUSCOv4 default configuration file.\n# Rename it as config.ini and edit the path and command values to match your own environnment.\n# You can use the script busco_configurator.py to do it for you\n# Many of the options in the busco_run section can alternatively be set using command line arguments. See the help prompt (busco -h) for details.\n# WARNING: passing a parameter through the command line overrides the value specified in this file.\n#\n# You need to set the path to this file in the environment variable BUSCO_CONFIG_FILE\n# as follows:\n# export BUSCO_CONFIG_FILE=\"/path/to/myconfig.ini\"\n#\n# Enable a parameter by removing \";\"\n#\n[busco_run]\n# Input file\n;in = /path/to/input_file.fna\n# Run name, used in output files and folder\n;out = BUSCO_run\n# Where to store the output directory\n;out_path = /path/to/output_folder\n# Path to the BUSCO dataset\n;lineage_dataset = bacteria\n# Which mode to run (genome / proteins / transcriptome)\n;mode = genome\n# Run lineage auto selector\n;auto-lineage = True\n# Run auto selector only for non-eukaryote datasets\n;auto-lineage-prok = True\n# Run auto selector only for eukaryote datasets\n;auto-lineage-euk = True\n# How many threads to use for multithreaded steps\n;cpu = 16\n# Force rewrite if files already exist (True/False)\n;force = False\n# Restart a previous BUSCO run (True/False)\n;restart = False\n# Blast e-value\n;evalue = 1e-3\n# How many candidate regions (contigs, scaffolds) to consider for each BUSCO\n;limit = 3\n# Augustus long mode for retraining (True/False)\n;long = False\n# Augustus species\n;augustus_species = human\n# Augustus parameters\n;augustus_parameters='--genemodel=intronless,--singlestrand=false'\n# Quiet mode (True/False)\n;quiet = False\n# Local destination path for downloaded lineage datasets\n;download_path = ./busco_downloads/\n# Run offline\n;offline=True\n# Ortho DB Datasets version\n;datasets_version = odb10\n# URL to BUSCO datasets\n;download_base_url = https://busco-data.ezlab.org/v4/data/\n# Download most recent BUSCO data and files\n;update-data = True\n\n[tblastn]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/ncbi-blast/2.9.0/bin/\ncommand = tblastn\n\n[makeblastdb]\npath =/opt/modules/biology/ncbi-blast/2.9.0/bin/\ncommand = makeblastdb\n\n[augustus]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/augustus/3.3.3/bin/\ncommand = augustus\n\n[etraining]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/augustus/3.3.3/bin/\ncommand = etraining\n\n[gff2gbSmallDNA.pl]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/augustus/3.3.3/scripts/\ncommand = gff2gbSmallDNA.pl\n\n[new_species.pl]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/augustus/3.3.3/scripts/\ncommand = new_species.pl\n\n[optimize_augustus.pl]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/augustus/3.3.3/scripts/\ncommand = optimize_augustus.pl\n\n[hmmsearch]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/hmmer/3.2.1/bin\ncommand = hmmsearch\n\n[sepp]\npath = /home/biodocker/sepp/\ncommand = run_sepp.py\n\n[prodigal]\npath = /opt/modules/biology/prodigal/2.6.3/bin/\ncommand = prodigal\n```"
