      "body": "The slurm command to view your job status is squeue, `squeue --me` being the most useful\n\n```\nusername@fortyfive /mnt/lfs2/username * sbatch sleep.slurm\nSubmitted batch job 1059141\nusername@fortyfive /mnt/lfs2/username * squeue --me\n             JOBID PARTITION     NAME     USER ST       TIME  NODES NODELIST(REASON)\n           1059141       reg sleep.sl username  R       0:05      1 n076\nusername@fortyfive /mnt/lfs2/username *\n```\n\nIf you leave off the '--me' flag all jobs in the queues are shown (this can be a long list)."
